  "query_preview": "..\nIssued 1151 PM CDT Thu Oct 22 2026\n\nSunday through Thursday:\n\nLow pressure passing by well to the northeast on Sunday will\ndrag a cold front through southern Wisconsin by the afternoon\nand/or evening hours. There should be enough time ahead of the\nfront for southerly winds through at least the first half of the\nday, so another mild day is expected. Winds will shift to\nnortherly behind the front later in the day, with cooler\nconditions then expected on Monday. Not expecting much moisture\nas this system moves through, so kept the dry forecast for\nSunday and Monday. \n\nTemps will remain cooler Tuesday, though likely still near or a\ncouple degrees above normal for late October. A shortwave will\nlift through the region Tuesday into Tuesday night, though the \nmain forcing and moisture is likely to remain north of the \nforecast area per latest models. Only have 10-20 percent chance \nfor rain in the northwest as this system slides by to the north.\n\n\n\n\nDDV",
